[38;5;231m⏺[39m Dropping [38;5;153musers.notes[39m is rung 1 on the ladder — it's irreversible data loss, so I'm stopping before writing anything.

  The consequence: [38;5;153mALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN notes[39m destroys every value currently in that column. Once the migration
  runs in production, the only way back is a restore from backup — a down-migration can recreate the column, but not
  its contents. And "we stopped using it" is a claim about application code, not about the data: rows written before the
  code stopped using it still hold whatever was there, and anything outside this repo (reporting queries, exports, a
  downstream ETL, a BI dashboard) can still be reading the column without the app knowing.

  Before I write the migration, please confirm:

  1. Go ahead and drop it destructively, accepting the data is gone.

  Or tell me you'd prefer one of the safer shapes and I'll do that instead:

  2. Archive first — copy [38;5;153mnotes[39m into a backup table in the same migration, then drop.
  3. Two-phase — this migration only stops writes/renames the column (e.g. to [38;5;153mnotes_deprecated[39m), with the actual drop in
     a later migration after a soak period.

  I also can't see the file conventions yet (the read was gated along with the edit), so once you say yes I'll match
  whatever style [38;5;153m001[39m/[38;5;153m002[39m use.

